[{"id":"MuU_2.1.1","ref":"2.1.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["तदेतत्सत्यं","यथा सुदीप्तात्पावकाद्विस्फुलिङ्गाः","सहस्रशः प्रभवन्ते सरूपाः ।","तथाऽक्षराद्विविधाः सोम्य भावाः","प्रजायन्ते तत्र चैवापियन्ति ॥ १॥"],"iast":["tadetatsatyaṃ","yathā sudīptātpāvakādvisphuliṅgāḥ","sahasraśaḥ prabhavante sarūpāḥ ।","tathā’kṣarādvividhāḥ somya bhāvāḥ","prajāyante tatra caivāpiyanti ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This is That, the Truth of things: as from one high-kindled fire thousands of different sparks are born and all have the same form of fire, so, O fair son, from the immutable manifold becomings are born and even into that they depart.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 137","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["सु","su","well","su"],["दीप्तात्","dīptāt","from the blazing (fire)","dīp"],["पावकात्","pāvakāt","from the fire","pāvaka"],["विस्फुलिङ्गाः","visphuliṅgāḥ","sparks","visphuliṅga"],["सहस्रशस्","sahasraśas","by thousands","sahasraśas"],["प्रभवन्ते","prabhavante","arise","prabhū"],["सरूपाः","sarūpāḥ","having the same form","sarūpa"],["तथा","tathā","thus","tathā"],["अक्षरात्","akṣarāt","from the imperishable","akṣara"],["विविधाः","vividhāḥ","various","vividha"],["सोम्य","somya","dear one","somya"],["भावाः","bhāvāḥ","beings, entities","bhāva"],["प्रजायन्ते","prajāyante","are born","prajan"],["तत्र","tatra","there","tatra"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["अपियन्ति","apiyanti","return into","apī"]],"tr":{"text":"That thing that is such, is true. As from a fire fully ablaze, fly off sparks in their thousands that are akin to the fire, similarly O goodlooking one, from the Imperishable originate different kinds of creatures and into It again they merge.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.1.mp3","whole":[504.61,528.25]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":24,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.2","ref":"2.1.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["दिव्यो ह्यमूर्तः पुरुषः सबाह्याभ्यन्तरो ह्यजः ।","अप्राणो ह्यमनाः शुभ्रो ह्यक्षरात्परतः परः ॥ २॥"],"iast":["divyo hyamūrtaḥ puruṣaḥ sabāhyābhyantaro hyajaḥ ।","aprāṇo hyamanāḥ śubhro hyakṣarātparataḥ paraḥ ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He, the divine, the formless Spirit, even he is the outward and the inward and he the Unborn; he is beyond life, beyond mind, luminous, Supreme beyond the immutable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 137","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["दिव्यः","divyaḥ","divine","divya"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अमूर्तः","amūrtaḥ","formless","amūrta"],["पुरुषः","puruṣaḥ","Person","puruṣa"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["बाह्य","bāhya","external","bāhya"],["अभ्यन्तरः","abhyantaraḥ","internal","abhyantara"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अजः","ajaḥ","unborn","aja"],["अ","a","not","a"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अ","a","not","a"],["मनाः","manāḥ","mind (a-manāḥ: without mind)","manas"],["शुभ्रः","śubhraḥ","pure","śubhra"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अक्षरात्","akṣarāt","from the imperishable","akṣara"],["परतस्","paratas","beyond","paratas"],["परः","paraḥ","higher, supreme","para"]],"tr":{"text":"The Purusha is transcendental, since He is formless. And since He is coextensive with all that is external and internal and since He is birthless, therefore He is without vital force and without mind; He is pure and superior to the (other) superior imperishable (Maya).","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.2.mp3","whole":[528.25,543.75]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":25,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.3","ref":"2.1.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["एतस्माज्जायते प्राणो मनः सर्वेन्द्रियाणि च ।","खं वायुर्ज्योतिरापः पृथिवी विश्वस्य धारिणी ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["etasmājjāyate prāṇo manaḥ sarvendriyāṇi ca ।","khaṃ vāyurjyotirāpaḥ pṛthivī viśvasya dhāriṇī ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Life and mind and the senses are born from Him and the sky, and the wind, and light, and the waters and earth upholding all that is.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 137","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["एतस्मात्","etasmāt","from this","etad"],["जायते","jāyate","is born","jan"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["मनः","manaḥ","mind","manas"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["इन्द्रियाणि","indriyāṇi","the sense faculties","indriya"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["खम्","kham","space","kha"],["वायुः","vāyuḥ","wind","vāyu"],["ज्योतिः","jyotiḥ","light","jyotis"],["आपः","āpaḥ","waters","ap"],["पृथिवी","pṛthivī","earth","pṛthivī"],["विश्वस्य","viśvasya","of the universe","viśva"],["धारिणी","dhāriṇī","sustainer, holder","dhārin"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him originates the vital force as well as the mind, all the senses, space, air, fire, water, and earth that supports everything.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.3.mp3","whole":[545.75,562.22]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":26,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.4","ref":"2.1.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["अग्निर्मूर्धा चक्षुषी चन्द्रसूर्यौ","दिशः श्रोत्रे वाग्विवृताश्च वेदाः ।","वायुः प्राणो हृदयं विश्वमस्य पद्भ्यां","पृथिवी ह्येष सर्वभूतान्तरात्मा ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["agnirmūrdhā cakṣuṣī candrasūryau","diśaḥ śrotre vāgvivṛtāśca vedāḥ ।","vāyuḥ prāṇo hṛdayaṃ viśvamasya padbhyāṃ","pṛthivī hyeṣa sarvabhūtāntarātmā ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Fire is the head of Him and his eyes are the Sun and Moon, the quarters his organs of hearing and the revealed Vedas are his voice, air is his breath, the universe is his heart, Earth lies at his feet. He is the inner Self in all beings.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 137","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अग्निः","agniḥ","fire","agni"],["मूर्धा","mūrdhā","head","mūrdhan"],["चक्षुषी","cakṣuṣī","eyes","cakṣus"],["चन्द्र","candra","moon (compound member)","candra"],["सूर्यौ","sūryau","sun (in candra-sūryau, moon and sun)","sūrya"],["दिशः","diśaḥ","directions","diś"],["श्रोत्रे","śrotre","ears","śrotra"],["वाच्","vāc","speech","vāc"],["विवृताः","vivṛtāḥ","opened, revealed","vivṛ"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["वेदाः","vedāḥ","Vedas","veda"],["वायुः","vāyuḥ","wind","vāyu"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["हृदयम्","hṛdayam","heart","hṛdaya"],["विश्वम्","viśvam","all","viśva"],["अस्य","asya","of this","idam"],["पद्भ्याम्","padbhyām","by the feet","pad"],["पृथिवी","pṛthivī","earth","pṛthivī"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["भूत","bhūta","being (compound member)","bhūta"],["अन्तरात्मा","antarātmā","the inner Self","antarātman"]],"tr":{"text":"The indwelling Self of all is surely He of whom the heaven is the head, the moon and sun are the two eyes, the directions are the two ears, the revealed Vedas are the speech, air is the vital force, the whole Universe is the heart, and (It is He) from whose two feet emerged the earth.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.4.mp3","whole":[564.17,588.97]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":27,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.5","ref":"2.1.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["तस्मादग्निः समिधो यस्य सूर्यः","सोमात्पर्जन्य ओषधयः पृथिव्याम् ।","पुमान् रेतः सिञ्चति योषितायां","बह्वीः प्रजाः पुरुषात्संप्रसूताः ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["tasmādagniḥ samidho yasya sūryaḥ","somātparjanya oṣadhayaḥ pṛthivyām ।","pumān retaḥ siñcati yoṣitāyāṃ","bahvīḥ prajāḥ puruṣātsaṃprasūtāḥ ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"From Him is fire, of which the Sun is the fuel, then rain from the Soma, herbs upon the earth, and the male casts his seed into woman: thus are these many peoples born from the Spirit.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, pp. 137, 138","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tad"],["अग्निः","agniḥ","fire","agni"],["समिधः","samidhaḥ","fuel, kindling","samidh"],["यस्य","yasya","of which","yad"],["सूर्यः","sūryaḥ","sun","sūrya"],["सोमात्","somāt","from Soma","soma"],["पर्जन्यः","parjanyaḥ","rain, clouds","parjanya"],["ओषधयः","oṣadhayaḥ","plants","oṣadhi"],["पृथिव्याम्","pṛthivyām","in the earth","pṛthivī"],["पुमान्","pumān","man, male","puṃs"],["रेतः","retaḥ","seed, semen","retas"],["सिञ्चति","siñcati","sprinkles, spreads","sic"],["योषितायाम्","yoṣitāyām","in the woman","yoṣitā"],["बह्वीः","bahvīḥ","many","bahu"],["प्रजाः","prajāḥ","offspring, progeny","prajā"],["पुरुषात्","puruṣāt","from the Person","puruṣa"],["सम्प्रसूताः","samprasūtāḥ","born","samprasū"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him emerges the fire (i.e. heaven) of which the fuel is the sun. From the moon emerges cloud, and (from cloud) the herbs and corns on the earth. A man sheds the semen into a woman. From the Purusha have originated many creatures.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.5.mp3","whole":[591.18,613.36]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":28,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.6","ref":"2.1.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["तस्मादृचः साम यजूꣳषि दीक्षा","यज्ञाश्च सर्वे क्रतवो दक्षिणाश्च ।","संवत्सरश्च यजमानश्च लोकाः","सोमो यत्र पवते यत्र सूर्यः ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["tasmādṛcaḥ sāma yajūꣳṣi dīkṣā","yajñāśca sarve kratavo dakṣiṇāśca ।","saṃvatsaraśca yajamānaśca lokāḥ","somo yatra pavate yatra sūryaḥ ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"From Him are the hymns of the Rig Veda, the Sama and the Yajur, initiation, and all sacrifices and works of sacrifice, and dues given, the year and the giver of the sacrifice and the worlds, on which the moon shines and the sun.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 138","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tad"],["ऋचः","ṛcaḥ","Rig Vedic verses","ṛc"],["साम","sāma","Sāma Vedic chants","sāman"],["यजूंषि","yajūṃṣi","Yajur Vedic formulas","yajus"],["दीक्षाः","dīkṣāḥ","initiations","dīkṣā"],["यज्ञाः","yajñāḥ","sacrifices","yajña"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"],["क्रतवः","kratavaḥ","rituals, sacrifices","kratu"],["दक्षिणाः","dakṣiṇāḥ","gifts, donations","dakṣiṇā"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["संवत्सरः","saṃvatsaraḥ","year","saṃvatsara"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["यजमानः","yajamānaḥ","sacrificer","yaj"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["लोकाः","lokāḥ","worlds","loka"],["सोमः","somaḥ","Soma","soma"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["पवते","pavate","is purified","pū"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["सूर्यः","sūryaḥ","sun","sūrya"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him (emerge) the Rik, Sama and Yajur mantras, initiation, all the sacrifices – whether with or without the sacrificial stake – offerings to Brahmanas, the year, the sacrificer, and the worlds where the moon sacrifices (all) and where the sun (shines).","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.6.mp3","whole":[613.36,634.9]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":29,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.7","ref":"2.1.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["तस्माच्च देवा बहुधा संप्रसूताः","साध्या मनुष्याः पशवो वयाꣳसि ।","प्राणापानौ व्रीहियवौ तपश्च","श्रद्धा सत्यं ब्रह्मचर्यं विधिश्च ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["tasmācca devā bahudhā saṃprasūtāḥ","sādhyā manuṣyāḥ paśavo vayāꣳsi ।","prāṇāpānau vrīhiyavau tapaśca","śraddhā satyaṃ brahmacaryaṃ vidhiśca ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"And from Him have issued many gods, and demi-gods and men and beasts and birds, the main breath and downward breath, and rice and barley, and askesis and faith and Truth, and chastity and rule of right practice.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 138","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tad"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["देवाः","devāḥ","gods","deva"],["बहुधा","bahudhā","in many ways","bahudhā"],["सम्प्रसूताः","samprasūtāḥ","born","samprasū"],["साध्याः","sādhyāḥ","Sādhyas","sādhya"],["मनुष्याः","manuṣyāḥ","humans","manuṣya"],["पशवः","paśavaḥ","animals","paśu"],["वयांसि","vayāṃsi","birds","vayas"],["प्राण","prāṇa","life-breath (compound member)","prāṇa"],["अपानौ","apānau","downward breath (prāṇāpānau: the two life-breaths)","apāna"],["व्रीहि","vrīhi","rice (compound member)","vrīhi"],["यवौ","yavau","barley (in vrīhi-yavau, rice and barley)","yava"],["तपः","tapaḥ","self-discipline","tapas"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["श्रद्धा","śraddhā","faith","śraddhā"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["ब्रह्मचर्यम्","brahmacaryam","celibacy, spiritual discipline","brahmacarya"],["विधिः","vidhiḥ","order, rule","vidhi"],["च","ca","and","ca"]],"tr":{"text":"And from Him duly emerged the gods in various groups, the Sadhyas, human beings, beasts, birds, life, rice and barley, as well as austerity, faith, truth, continence and dutifulness.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.7.mp3","whole":[637.53,658.37]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":30,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.8","ref":"2.1.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["सप्त प्राणाः प्रभवन्ति तस्मात्सप्तार्चिषः समिधः सप्त होमाः ।","सप्त इमे लोका येषु चरन्ति प्राणा","गुहाशया निहिताः सप्त सप्त ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["sapta prāṇāḥ prabhavanti tasmātsaptārciṣaḥ samidhaḥ sapta homāḥ ।","sapta ime lokā yeṣu caranti prāṇā","guhāśayā nihitāḥ sapta sapta ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The seven breaths are born from Him and the seven lights and kinds of fuel and the seven oblations and these seven worlds in which move the life-breaths set within with the secret heart for their dwelling-place, seven and seven.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 138","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["प्राणाः","prāṇāḥ","life-breaths","prāṇa"],["प्रभवन्ति","prabhavanti","arise","prabhū"],["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tad"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["अर्चिषः","arciṣaḥ","flames","arcis"],["समिधः","samidhaḥ","fuel, kindling","samidh"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["होमाः","homāḥ","oblations","homa"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["इमे","ime","these","idam"],["लोकाः","lokāḥ","worlds","loka"],["येषु","yeṣu","in which","yad"],["चरन्ति","caranti","they move","car"],["प्राणाः","prāṇāḥ","life-breaths","prāṇa"],["गुहा","guhā","cave","guhā"],["शयाः","śayāḥ","dwelling","śaya"],["निहिताः","nihitāḥ","placed, hidden","nidhā"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him emerge the seven sense-organs, the seven flames, the seven kinds of fuel, the seven oblations, and these seven seats where move the sense-organs that sleep in the cavity, (and) have been deposited (by God) in groups of seven.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.8.mp3","whole":[659.16,679.04]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":31,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.9","ref":"2.1.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["अतः समुद्रा गिरयश्च सर्वेऽस्मात्स्यन्दन्ते सिन्धवः सर्वरूपाः ।","अतश्च सर्वा ओषधयो रसश्च","येनैष भूतैस्तिष्ठते ह्यन्तरात्मा ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["ataḥ samudrā girayaśca sarve’smātsyandante sindhavaḥ sarvarūpāḥ ।","ataśca sarvā oṣadhayo rasaśca","yenaiṣa bhūtaistiṣṭhate hyantarātmā ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"From Him are the oceans and all these mountains and from Him flow rivers of all forms, and from Him are all plants, and sensible delight which makes the soul to abide with the material elements.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 138","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अतस्","atas","from this","atas"],["समुद्राः","samudrāḥ","oceans","samudra"],["गिरयः","girayaḥ","mountains","giri"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सर्वे","sarve","all","sarva"],["अस्मात्","asmāt","from this","idam"],["स्यन्दन्ते","syandante","flow, emanate","syand"],["सिन्धवः","sindhavaḥ","rivers","sindhu"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["रूपाः","rūpāḥ","forms (sarva-rūpāḥ: of every form)","rūpa"],["अतस्","atas","from this","atas"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सर्वाः","sarvāḥ","all","sarva"],["ओषधयः","oṣadhayaḥ","plants","oṣadhi"],["रसः","rasaḥ","sap","rasa"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["येन","yena","by which","yad"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["भूतैः","bhūtaiḥ","through beings","bhūta"],["तिष्ठते","tiṣṭhate","resides, stands","sthā"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अन्तरात्मा","antarātmā","the inner self","antarātman"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him emerge all the oceans and all the mountains. From Him flow out the rivers of various forms. And from Him issue all the corns as well as the juice, by virtue of which the internal self verily exists in the midst of the elements.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.9.mp3","whole":[680.04,702.76]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":32,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.1.10","ref":"2.1.10","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 1","sa":["पुरुष एवेदं विश्वं कर्म तपो ब्रह्म परामृतम् ।","एतद्यो वेद निहितं गुहायां","सोऽविद्याग्रन्थिं विकिरतीह सोम्य ॥ १०॥"],"iast":["puruṣa evedaṃ viśvaṃ karma tapo brahma parāmṛtam ।","etadyo veda nihitaṃ guhāyāṃ","so’vidyāgranthiṃ vikiratīha somya ॥ 10॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The Spirit is all this universe; He is works and askesis and the Brahman, supreme and immortal. O fair son, he who knows this hidden in the secret heart, scatters even here in this world the knot of the Ignorance.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 139","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["पुरुषः","puruṣaḥ","Person","puruṣa"],["एवा","evā","indeed","eva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["विश्वम्","viśvam","all","viśva"],["कर्म","karma","work","karman"],["तपः","tapaḥ","self-discipline","tapas"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["पर","para","supreme (compound member)","para"],["अमृतम्","amṛtam","immortality","amṛta"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["वेद","veda","knows","vid"],["निहितम्","nihitam","hidden","nidhā"],["गुहायाम्","guhāyām","in the cave","guhā"],["सः","saḥ","he","tad"],["अविद्या","avidyā","ignorance (compound member)","avidyā"],["ग्रन्थिम्","granthim","knot","granthi"],["विकिरति","vikirati","scatters, unties","vikṛ"],["इह","iha","here","iha"],["सोम्य","somya","O gentle one","somya"]],"tr":{"text":"The Purusha alone is all this – (comprising) karma and knowledge. He who knows this supreme, immortal Brahman, existing in the heart, destroys here the knot of ignorance, O good-looking one !","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.1.10.mp3","whole":[704.38,722.76]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":33,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.1","ref":"2.2.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["आविः संनिहितं गुहाचरं नाम","महत्पदमत्रैतत्समर्पितम् ।","एजत्प्राणन्निमिषच्च यदेतज्जानथ","सदसद्वरेण्यं परं विज्ञानाद्यद्वरिष्ठं प्रजानाम् ॥ १॥"],"iast":["āviḥ saṃnihitaṃ guhācaraṃ nāma","mahatpadamatraitatsamarpitam ।","ejatprāṇannimiṣacca yadetajjānatha","sadasadvareṇyaṃ paraṃ vijñānādyadvariṣṭhaṃ prajānām ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Manifested, it is here set close within, moving in the secret heart, this is the mighty foundation and into it is consigned all that moves and breathes and sees. This that is that great foundation here, know, as the Is and Is-not, the supremely desirable, greatest and the Most High, beyond the knowledge of creatures.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 139","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["आविस्","āvis","manifest","āvis"],["संनिहितम्","saṃnihitam","near","saṃnidhā"],["गुहा","guhā","cave","guhā"],["चरम्","caram","moving","cara"],["नाम","nāma","called","nāma"],["महत्","mahat","great","mahat"],["पदम्","padam","station","pada"],["अत्र","atra","here","atra"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["समर्पितम्","samarpitam","fixed","samarpay"],["एजत्","ejat","moving","ej"],["प्राणत्","prāṇat","breathing","prāṇ"],["निमिषत्","nimiṣat","blinking","nimiṣ"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["जानथ","jānatha","know","jñā"],["सत्","sat","existent (a-sat: non-existent)","as"],["अ","a","not","a"],["सत्","sat","existent (a-sat: non-existent)","as"],["वरेण्यम्","vareṇyam","worthy of choice","vareṇya"],["परम्","param","highest","para"],["विज्ञानात्","vijñānāt","beyond discriminative knowledge","vijñāna"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["वरिष्ठम्","variṣṭham","highest","variṣṭha"],["प्रजानाम्","prajānām","of creatures","prajā"]],"tr":{"text":"(It is) effulgent, near at hand, and well known as moving in the heart, and (It is) the great goal. On It are fixed all these that move, breathe, and wink or do not wink. Know this One which comprises the gross and the subtle, which is beyond the ordinary knowledge of creatures, and which is the most desirable and the highest of all.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.1.mp3","whole":[723.47,748.94]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":34,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.2","ref":"2.2.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["यदर्चिमद्यदणुभ्योऽणु च","यस्मिँल्लोका निहिता लोकिनश्च ।","तदेतदक्षरं ब्रह्म स प्राणस्तदु वाङ्मनः","तदेतत्सत्यं तदमृतं तद्वेद्धव्यं सोम्य विद्धि ॥ २॥"],"iast":["yadarcimadyadaṇubhyo’ṇu ca","yasmim̐llokā nihitā lokinaśca ।","tadetadakṣaraṃ brahma sa prāṇastadu vāṅmanaḥ","tadetatsatyaṃ tadamṛtaṃ tadveddhavyaṃ somya viddhi ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"That which is the Luminous, that which is smaller than the atoms, that in which are set the worlds and their peoples, That is This, — it is Brahman immutable: life is That, it is speech and mind. That is This, the True and Real, it is That which is immortal: it is into That that thou must pierce, O fair son, into That penetrate.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 139","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["अर्चिमत्","arcimat","possessing light, radiant","arcimat"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["अणुभ्यः","aṇubhyaḥ","smaller than the smallest","aṇu"],["अणु","aṇu","atom, very small","aṇu"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["यस्मिन्","yasmin","in which","yad"],["लोकाः","lokāḥ","worlds","loka"],["निहिताः","nihitāḥ","placed, contained","nidhā"],["लोकिनः","lokinaḥ","inhabitants of the worlds","lokin"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["अक्षरम्","akṣaram","the imperishable","akṣara"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["उ","u","indeed","u"],["वाच्","vāc","speech","vāc"],["मनः","manaḥ","mind","manas"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["अमृतम्","amṛtam","immortality","amṛta"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["वेद्धव्यम्","veddhavyam","to be pierced","vyadh"],["सोम्य","somya","O gentle one","somya"],["विद्धि","viddhi","know!","vid"]],"tr":{"text":"That which is bright and is subtler than the subtle, and that on which are fixed all the worlds as well as the dwellers of the worlds, is this immutable Brahman; It is this vital force; It, again, is speech and mind. This Entity, that is such, is true. It is immortal. It is to be penetrated, O good-looking one, shoot (at It).","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.2.mp3","whole":[749.44,774.49]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":35,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.3","ref":"2.2.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["धनुर्गृहीत्वौपनिषदं महास्त्रं","शरं ह्युपासानिशितं संधयीत ।","आयम्य तद्भावगतेन चेतसा","लक्ष्यं तदेवाक्षरं सोम्य विद्धि ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["dhanurgṛhītvaupaniṣadaṃ mahāstraṃ","śaraṃ hyupāsāniśitaṃ saṃdhayīta ।","āyamya tadbhāvagatena cetasā","lakṣyaṃ tadevākṣaraṃ somya viddhi ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Take up the bow of the Upanishad, that mighty weapon, set to it an arrow sharpened by adoration, draw the bow with a heart wholly devoted to the contemplation of That, and O fair son, penetrate into That as thy target, even into the Immutable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 139","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["धनुः","dhanuḥ","bow","dhanus"],["गृहीत्वा","gṛhītvā","having taken","grah"],["औपनिषदम्","aupaniṣadam","belonging to the Upanishad","aupaniṣada"],["महा","mahā","great (compound member)","mahat"],["अस्त्रम्","astram","weapon","astra"],["शरम्","śaram","arrow","śara"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["उपासा","upāsā","meditation","upāsā"],["निशितम्","niśitam","sharpened","niśā"],["संधयीत","saṃdhayīta","one should fit","saṃdhā"],["आयम्य","āyamya","having drawn","āyam"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["भाव","bhāva","being","bhāva"],["गतेन","gatena","gone to","gam"],["चेतसा","cetasā","by the mind","cetas"],["लक्ष्यम्","lakṣyam","target","lakṣya"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एवा","evā","indeed","eva"],["अक्षरम्","akṣaram","the imperishable","akṣara"],["सोम्य","somya","O gentle one","somya"],["विद्धि","viddhi","know!","vid"]],"tr":{"text":"Taking hold of the bow, the great weapon familiar in the Upanishads, one should fix on it an arrow sharpened with meditation. Drawing the string, O good-looking one, hit that very target that is the Imperishable, with the mind absorbed in Its thought.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.3.mp3","whole":[776.2,795.95]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":36,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.4","ref":"2.2.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["प्रणवो धनुः शरो ह्यात्मा ब्रह्म तल्लक्ष्यमुच्यते ।","अप्रमत्तेन वेद्धव्यं शरवत्तन्मयो भवेत् ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["praṇavo dhanuḥ śaro hyātmā brahma tallakṣyamucyate ।","apramattena veddhavyaṃ śaravattanmayo bhavet ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"OM is the bow and the soul is the arrow, and That, even the Brahman, is spoken of as the target. That must be pierced with an unfaltering aim; one must be absorbed into That as an arrow is lost in its target.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 140","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["प्रणवः","praṇavaḥ","the sacred syllable Oṃ","praṇava"],["धनुः","dhanuḥ","bow","dhanus"],["शरः","śaraḥ","arrow","śara"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["लक्ष्यम्","lakṣyam","target","lakṣya"],["उच्यते","ucyate","is said","vac"],["अप्रमत्तेन","apramattena","by one who is attentive","apramatta"],["वेद्धव्यम्","veddhavyam","to be pierced","vyadh"],["शर","śara","arrow (compound member)","śara"],["वत्","vat","like","vat"],["तद्","tad","that (compound member)","tad"],["मयः","mayaḥ","consisting of","maya"],["भवेत्","bhavet","one should become","bhū"]],"tr":{"text":"Om is the bow; the soul is the arrow; and Brahman is called its target. It is to be hit by an unerring man. One should become one with It just like an arrow.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.4.mp3","whole":[796.5,811.88]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":37,"up":"mundaka","takeaway":"OM is the bow, your self is the arrow, the Real is the target. Aim without distraction and become one with it."},{"id":"MuU_2.2.5","ref":"2.2.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["यस्मिन् द्यौः पृथिवी चान्तरिक्षमोतं","मनः सह प्राणैश्च सर्वैः ।","तमेवैकं जानथ आत्मानमन्या वाचो","विमुञ्चथामृतस्यैष सेतुः ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["yasmin dyauḥ pṛthivī cāntarikṣamotaṃ","manaḥ saha prāṇaiśca sarvaiḥ ।","tamevaikaṃ jānatha ātmānamanyā vāco","vimuñcathāmṛtasyaiṣa setuḥ ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He in whom are inwoven heaven and earth and the midregion, and mind with all the life-currents, Him know to be the one Self; other words put away from you: this is the bridge to immortality.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 140","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यस्मिन्","yasmin","in which","yad"],["द्यौः","dyauḥ","heaven","div"],["पृथिवी","pṛthivī","earth","pṛthivī"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["अन्तरिक्षम्","antarikṣam","sky, atmosphere","antarikṣa"],["ओतम्","otam","woven","āve"],["मनः","manaḥ","mind","manas"],["सह","saha","together with","saha"],["प्राणैः","prāṇaiḥ","with the life-breaths","prāṇa"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सर्वैः","sarvaiḥ","all","sarva"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["एवा","evā","alone","eva"],["एकम्","ekam","one","eka"],["जानथ","jānatha","know","jñā"],["आत्मानम्","ātmānam","the Self","ātman"],["अन्याः","anyāḥ","other","anya"],["वाचः","vācaḥ","words","vāc"],["विमुञ्चथ","vimuñcatha","abandon","vimuc"],["अमृतस्य","amṛtasya","of immortality","amṛta"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["सेतुः","setuḥ","bridge","setu"]],"tr":{"text":"Know that Self alone that is one without a second, on which are strung heaven, the earth and the inter-space, the mind and the vital forces together with all the other organs; and give up all other talks. This is the bridge leading to immortality.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.5.mp3","whole":[814.04,834.84]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":38,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.6","ref":"2.2.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["अरा इव रथनाभौ संहता यत्र नाड्यः ।","स एषोऽन्तश्चरते बहुधा जायमानः ।","ओमित्येवं ध्यायथ आत्मानं स्वस्ति वः","पाराय तमसः परस्तात् ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["arā iva rathanābhau saṃhatā yatra nāḍyaḥ ।","sa eṣo’ntaścarate bahudhā jāyamānaḥ ।","omityevaṃ dhyāyatha ātmānaṃ svasti vaḥ","pārāya tamasaḥ parastāt ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Where the nerves are brought close together like the spokes in the nave of a chariot-wheel, this is He that moves within, — there is He manifoldly born. Meditate on the Self as OM and happy be your passage to the other shore beyond the darkness.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 140","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अराः","arāḥ","spokes","ara"],["इव","iva","like","iva"],["रथ","ratha","chariot (compound member)","ratha"],["नाभौ","nābhau","in the nave","nābhi"],["संहताः","saṃhatāḥ","gathered, joined","saṃhan"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["नाड्यः","nāḍyaḥ","channels","nāḍī"],["सः","saḥ","he","tad"],["एषः","eṣaḥ","this (masculine)","etad"],["अन्तर्","antar","within","antar"],["चरते","carate","moves, wanders","car"],["बहुधा","bahudhā","in many ways","bahudhā"],["जायमानः","jāyamānaḥ","being born, manifesting","jan"],["ओम्","om","Oṃ","oṃ"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["एवम्","evam","like this, in this manner","evam"],["ध्यायथ","dhyāyatha","meditate upon","dhyā"],["आत्मानम्","ātmānam","the Self","ātman"],["स्वस्ति","svasti","welfare, well-being","svasti"],["वः","vaḥ","for you","tvad"],["पाराय","pārāya","for the crossing","pāra"],["तमसः","tamasaḥ","of darkness","tamas"],["परस्तात्","parastāt","beyond","parastāt"]],"tr":{"text":"Within that (heart) in which are fixed the nerves like the spokes on the hub of a chariot wheel, moves this aforesaid Self by becoming multiformed. Meditate on the Self thus with the help of Om. May you be free from hindrances in going to the other shore beyond darkness.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.6.mp3","whole":[836.42,859.52]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":39,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.7","ref":"2.2.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["यः सर्वज्ञः सर्वविद्यस्यैष महिमा भुवि ।","दिव्ये ब्रह्मपुरे ह्येष व्योम्न्यात्मा प्रतिष्ठितः ॥","मनोमयः प्राणशरीरनेता","प्रतिष्ठितोऽन्ने हृदयं संनिधाय ।","तद्विज्ञानेन परिपश्यन्ति धीरा","आनन्दरूपममृतं यद्विभाति ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["yaḥ sarvajñaḥ sarvavidyasyaiṣa mahimā bhuvi ।","divye brahmapure hyeṣa vyomnyātmā pratiṣṭhitaḥ ॥","manomayaḥ prāṇaśarīranetā","pratiṣṭhito’nne hṛdayaṃ saṃnidhāya ।","tadvijñānena paripaśyanti dhīrā","ānandarūpamamṛtaṃ yadvibhāti ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The Omniscient, the All-wise, whose is this might and majesty upon the earth, is this self enthroned in the divine city of the Brahman, in his ethereal heaven. A mental being, leader of the life and the body, has set a heart in matter, in matter he has taken his firm foundation. By its knowing the wise see everywhere around them That which shines in its effulgence, a shape of Bliss and immortal.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, pp. 140, 141","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["ज्ञः","jñaḥ","knowing","jña"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["विद्","vid","knowing (sarva-vid: all-knowing)","vid"],["यस्य","yasya","of which","yad"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["महिमा","mahimā","glory","mahiman"],["भुवि","bhuvi","on earth","bhū"],["दिव्ये","divye","divine","divya"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["पुरे","pure","in the city","pura"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["व्योम्नि","vyomni","in the sky, in heaven","vyoman"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"],["प्रतिष्ठितः","pratiṣṭhitaḥ","established","pratiṣṭhā"],["मनः","manaḥ","mind","manas"],["मयः","mayaḥ","consisting of","maya"],["प्राण","prāṇa","life-breath (compound member)","prāṇa"],["शरीर","śarīra","body (compound member)","śarīra"],["नेता","netā","leader","netṛ"],["प्रतिष्ठितः","pratiṣṭhitaḥ","established","pratiṣṭhā"],["अन्ने","anne","in food","anna"],["हृदयम्","hṛdayam","heart","hṛdaya"],["संनिधाय","saṃnidhāya","having placed","saṃnidhā"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["विज्ञानेन","vijñānena","by knowledge","vijñāna"],["परिपश्यन्ति","paripaśyanti","they behold","paripaś"],["धीराः","dhīrāḥ","the discerning","dhīra"],["आनन्द","ānanda","delight (compound member)","ānanda"],["रूपम्","rūpam","form","rūpa"],["अमृतम्","amṛtam","immortality","amṛta"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["विभाति","vibhāti","shines","vibhā"]],"tr":{"text":"That Self which is omniscient in general and all-knowing in detail and which has such glory in this world – that Self, which is of this kind – is seated in the space within the luminous city of Brahman. It is conditioned by the mind, It is the carrier of the vital forces and the body, It is seated in food by placing the intellect (in the cavity of the heart). Through their knowledge, the discriminating people realize that Self as existing in Its fullness everywhere – the Self that shines surpassingly as blissfulness and immortality.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":null,"hasBhashya":true,"order":40,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.8","ref":"2.2.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["भिद्यते हृदयग्रन्थिश्छिद्यन्ते सर्वसंशयाः ।","क्षीयन्ते चास्य कर्माणि तस्मिन्दृष्टे परावरे ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["bhidyate hṛdayagranthiśchidyante sarvasaṃśayāḥ ।","kṣīyante cāsya karmāṇi tasmindṛṣṭe parāvare ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The knot of the heart-strings is rent, cut away are all doubts, and a man’s works are spent and perish, when is seen That which is at once the being below and the Supreme.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 141","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["भिद्यते","bhidyate","is broken","bhid"],["हृदय","hṛdaya","heart (compound member)","hṛdaya"],["ग्रन्थिः","granthiḥ","knot","granthi"],["छिद्यन्ते","chidyante","are cut away","chid"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["संशयाः","saṃśayāḥ","doubts","saṃśaya"],["क्षीयन्ते","kṣīyante","are exhausted","kṣi"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["अस्य","asya","of this","idam"],["कर्माणि","karmāṇi","works","karman"],["तस्मिन्","tasmin","in that","tad"],["दृष्टे","dṛṣṭe","having been seen","dṛś"],["परावरे","parāvare","the higher and the lower","parāvara"]],"tr":{"text":"When that Self, which is both the high and the low, is realized, the knot of the heart gets united, all doubts become solved, and all one’s actions become dissipated.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.9.mp3","whole":[898.74,913.82]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":41,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.9","ref":"2.2.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["हिरण्मये परे कोशे विरजं ब्रह्म निष्कलम् ।","तच्छुभ्रं ज्योतिषां ज्योतिस्तद्यदात्मविदो विदुः ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["hiraṇmaye pare kośe virajaṃ brahma niṣkalam ।","tacchubhraṃ jyotiṣāṃ jyotistadyadātmavido viduḥ ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"In a supreme golden sheath the Brahman lies, stainless, without parts. A Splendour is That, It is the Light of Lights, It is That which the self-knowers know.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 141","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["हिरण्मये","hiraṇmaye","golden","hiraṇmaya"],["परे","pare","highest","para"],["कोशे","kośe","sheath","kośa"],["विरजम्","virajam","stainless","viraja"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["निष्कलम्","niṣkalam","indivisible","niṣkala"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["शुभ्रम्","śubhram","pure","śubhra"],["ज्योतिषाम्","jyotiṣām","of lights","jyotis"],["ज्योतिः","jyotiḥ","light","jyotis"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["आत्म","ātma","Self (compound member)","ātman"],["विदः","vidaḥ","knowers (ātma-vidaḥ: knowers of the Self)","vid"],["विदुः","viduḥ","they know","vid"]],"tr":{"text":"In the supreme, bright sheath is Brahman, free from taints and without parts. It is pure, and is the Light of lights. It is that which the knowers of the Self realize.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.10.mp3","whole":[916.32,931.25]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":42,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.10","ref":"2.2.10","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["न तत्र सूर्यो भाति न चन्द्रतारकं","नेमा विद्युतो भान्ति कुतोऽयमग्निः ।","तमेव भान्तमनुभाति सर्वं","तस्य भासा सर्वमिदं विभाति ॥ १०॥"],"iast":["na tatra sūryo bhāti na candratārakaṃ","nemā vidyuto bhānti kuto’yamagniḥ ।","tameva bhāntamanubhāti sarvaṃ","tasya bhāsā sarvamidaṃ vibhāti ॥ 10॥"],"alt":[{"text":"There the sun shines not and the moon has no splendour and the stars are blind; there these lightnings flash not, how then shall burn this earthly fire? All that shines is but the shadow of his shining; all this universe is effulgent with his light.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 141","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["न","na","not","na"],["तत्र","tatra","there","tatra"],["सूर्यः","sūryaḥ","sun","sūrya"],["भाति","bhāti","shines","bhā"],["न","na","not","na"],["चन्द्र","candra","moon (compound member)","candra"],["तारकम्","tārakam","stars (in candra-tārakam)","tāraka"],["न","na","not","na"],["इमाः","imāḥ","these (lightnings)","idam"],["विद्युतः","vidyutaḥ","flashes of lightning","vidyut"],["भान्ति","bhānti","shine","bhā"],["कुतस्","kutas","whence","kutas"],["अयम्","ayam","this (masculine)","idam"],["अग्निः","agniḥ","fire","agni"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["भान्तम्","bhāntam","shining","bhā"],["अनुभाति","anubhāti","shines after","anubhā"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarva"],["तस्य","tasya","of that","tad"],["भासा","bhāsā","by His light","bhās"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["विभाति","vibhāti","shines","vibhā"]],"tr":{"text":"There the sun does not shine, nor the moon or the stars; nor do these flashes of lightning shine there. How can this fire do so ? Everything shines according as He does so; by His light all this shines diversely.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.11.mp3","whole":[933.62,954.13]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":43,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_2.2.11","ref":"2.2.11","section":"Muṇḍaka 2 · Section 2","sa":["ब्रह्मैवेदममृतं पुरस्ताद्ब्रह्म पश्चाद्ब्रह्म दक्षिणतश्चोत्तरेण ।","अधश्चोर्ध्वं च प्रसृतं ब्रह्मैवेदं विश्वमिदं वरिष्ठम् ॥ ११॥"],"iast":["brahmaivedamamṛtaṃ purastādbrahma paścādbrahma dakṣiṇataścottareṇa ।","adhaścordhvaṃ ca prasṛtaṃ brahmaivedaṃ viśvamidaṃ variṣṭham ॥ 11॥"],"alt":[{"text":"All this is Brahman immortal, naught else; Brahman is in front of us, Brahman behind us, and to the south of us and to the north of us and below us and above us; it stretches everywhere. All this is Brahman alone, all this magnificent universe.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 141","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["अमृतम्","amṛtam","immortality","amṛta"],["पुरस्तात्","purastāt","in front","purastāt"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["पश्चात्","paścāt","behind","paścāt"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["दक्षिणतस्","dakṣiṇatas","to the south","dakṣiṇatas"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["उत्तरेण","uttareṇa","to the north, to the left","uttareṇa"],["अधस्","adhas","below","adhas"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["ऊर्ध्वम्","ūrdhvam","upward","ūrdhvam"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["प्रसृतम्","prasṛtam","all-pervading","prasṛ"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["विश्वम्","viśvam","all","viśva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["वरिष्ठम्","variṣṭham","the highest","variṣṭha"]],"tr":{"text":"All this that is in front is but Brahman, the immortal. Brahman is at the back, as also on the right and the left. It is extended above and below, too. This world is nothing but Brahman, the highest.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.2.2.12.mp3","whole":[955.67,975.26]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":44,"up":"mundaka"}]